  "text": "The Philippine City Disaster Insurance Pool (PCDIP) is a proposed parametric catastrophe insurance program aimed at providing rapid and cost-effective payouts to Philippine cities after severe disasters. Supported by the Asian Development Bank and the Philippine Department of Finance, it targets medium-to-high severity earthquakes and typhoons, addressing the immediate post-disaster liquidity gap at the local government unit level.",
